index 0000000..e2aead8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/HEGEL_REPORT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@
+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report — openraft
+
+Target: `openraft` 0.10.0-alpha.30 (workspace member `openraft/`), commit `0d15d99`.
+Setup: `cargo add --dev hegeltest -p openraft` (hegeltest 0.28.2, toolchain nightly-2026-03-01, edition 2024) — worked first try.
+
+Per the task guidance, full multi-node consensus simulation was skipped in favor of the
+deterministic sans-IO pieces: quorum logic, joint-consensus membership change, vote/log-id
+ordering, and the commit-index progress tracker. All tests are unit tests added to the
+existing in-crate test files/modules.
+
+## Properties tested
+
+16 hegel tests (15 distinct properties plus 1 pinned known-failure reproducer).
+
+### `openraft/src/quorum/quorum_set_test.rs`
+
+1. **`hegel_majority_quorum_matches_counting_oracle`** — `BTreeSet<u64>::is_quorum`
+   agrees with an independent counting oracle (`|granted ∩ config| * 2 > |config|`),
+   and the `&[ID]` implementation agrees with the `BTreeSet` one. Ids drawn from a
+   small pool mixed with full-range `u64` boundaries.
+2. **`hegel_joint_quorum_is_majority_in_every_config`** — `Vec<BTreeSet<u64>>::is_quorum`
+   is true iff the granted set is a majority (per the oracle) in *every* config.
+3. **`hegel_quorum_is_upward_closed`** — documented trait requirement: adding ids to a
+   quorum yields a quorum (granted sets biased toward member subsets to avoid vacuity).
+
+### `openraft/src/quorum/coherent_test.rs`
+
+4. **`hegel_find_coherent_yields_pairwise_intersecting_quorums`** — the membership-change
+   safety property: for joint config `A` and goal `B`, `X = A.find_coherent(B)` satisfies
+   `A ~ X ~ B`, checked against an *exhaustive* enumeration of all quorums over a 7-node
+   universe (every quorum of `A` intersects every quorum of `X`, and likewise `X`/`B`).
+5. **`hegel_is_coherent_with_implies_intersecting_quorums`** — soundness of the
+   shared-config coherence check against the same exhaustive intersection oracle
+   (coherent pairs forced half the time by copying a config across).
+
+### `openraft/src/membership/membership_test.rs`
+
+6. **`hegel_next_coherent_reaches_goal_within_two_steps`** — documented contract of
+   `Membership::next_coherent`: iterating toward a goal reaches the uniform goal config in
+   two steps, and each step is coherent with the previous one.
+7. **`hegel_membership_change_yields_valid_coherent_membership`** — for arbitrary valid
+   memberships and arbitrary `ChangeMembers` requests (all 8 variants plus `Batch`),
+   a successful `change()` yields a membership that passes `ensure_valid()`, whose configs
+   are coherent with the old configs, and whose voters/learners partition the node set.
+8. **`hegel_membership_serde_roundtrip`** (`--features serde`) — JSON round-trip of valid
+   `Membership<u64, ()>`.
+
+### `openraft/src/vote/vote.rs` (`mod hegel_props`)
+
+9. **`hegel_adv_vote_order_matches_tuple_oracle`** — `Vote<leader_id_adv::LeaderId>` is
+   totally ordered and matches the lexicographic `(term, node_id, committed)` oracle.
+10. **`hegel_std_vote_partial_cmp_duality`** — for `Vote<leader_id_std::LeaderId>`,
+    `partial_cmp(a, b)` is the reverse of `partial_cmp(b, a)`, and `Some(Equal)`
+    coincides with `==`.
+11. **`hegel_std_vote_partial_cmp_transitive`** — transitivity of `<=`/`>=` over generated
+    triples (exercises the subtle "committed wins between incomparable leader ids" rule in
+    `RefVote::partial_cmp`).
+12. **`hegel_std_vote_partial_cmp_no_panic_on_full_domain`** — comparing publicly
+    constructible votes never panics. **Found a real panic**; the known-buggy input class
+    (equal terms with `voted_for: None`) is excluded with a comment referencing the pin:
+13. **`hegel_std_vote_partial_cmp_none_voted_for_panics`** — KNOWN FAILURE pin for the
+    bug below; fails deterministically on every generated case.
+14. **`hegel_vote_serde_roundtrip`** (`--features serde`) — JSON round-trip for both
+    leader-id flavors, including `voted_for: None`.
+
+### `openraft/src/log_id/mod.rs` (`mod hegel_props`)
+
+15. **`hegel_log_id_order_matches_tuple_oracle`** — the module-doc ordering promise:
+    adv log ids order as `(term, node_id, index)`, std log ids as `(term, index)`
+    (guards against field-reorder breaking the derived `Ord`).
+
+### `openraft/src/progress/vec_progress.rs` (inside existing `mod tests`)
+
+16. **`hegel_vec_progress_matches_reference_model`** — model test for the commit-index
+    tracker: generated sequences of `update` (monotonic), `increase_to` (arbitrary,
+    self-clamping), unknown-id updates, and `upgrade_quorum_set` — with the joint quorum
+    configurations themselves generated, not canned — agree after every step with the
+    existing straightforward reference model (`model_quorum_accepted`) and preserve the
+    internal sorted-voter-prefix invariant. This evolves the existing seeded-LCG model
+    tests (kept in place); hegel now controls the randomness so failures shrink.
+
+## Test results
+
+- `cargo test -p openraft --lib --features serde`: **558 passed, 1 failed** — the only
+  failure is the deterministic KNOWN FAILURE pin (`hegel_std_vote_partial_cmp_none_voted_for_panics`).
+  Default-features run: 546 passed, same single pinned failure.
+- Liveness check: temporarily inverted the joint-quorum assertion; hegel reported a
+  correctly shrunk counterexample (`joint = [{0}]`, `granted = {}`). Reverted.
+- Exploratory 10x run (`test_cases = 1000` on all 16 tests, with `serde`): no additional
+  failures; total wall time ~1.4 s. Reverted to default counts.
+- `cargo clippy --no-deps -p openraft --all-targets -- -D warnings` (both with and without
+  `serde`): clean. Note: the repo's `make lint` cannot complete in this environment — its
+  workspace-wide clippy step fails building `openssl-sys` (no OpenSSL headers installed)
+  in an unrelated workspace member, before ever reaching openraft. The `cargo fmt` steps
+  of `make lint` did run. This is a pre-existing environment limitation, not caused by
+  these changes.
+- `.hegel/` added to `.gitignore`.
+
+## Suspected bugs
+
+### 1. `Vote`/`LeaderId` comparison panics when `voted_for` is `None` (std leader id)
+
+- **Where:** `openraft/src/vote/leader_id/leader_id_std.rs:134` —
+  `RaftLeaderId::node_id()` is `self.voted_for.as_ref().unwrap()`, reached from
+  `LeaderIdCompare::std` (`openraft/src/vote/leader_id/leader_id_cmp.rs`) whenever two
+  leader ids have equal terms.
+- **Reproducer (minimal, found and shrunk by hegel):**
+  ```rust
+  use openraft::impls::leader_id_std::LeaderId;
+  use openraft::Vote;
+  let a = Vote::<LeaderId<u64, u64>> {
+      leader_id: LeaderId { term: 0, voted_for: None },
+      committed: false,
+  };
+  let _ = a.partial_cmp(&a.clone()); // panics: called `Option::unwrap()` on a `None` value
+  ```
+- **Why it looks real:** `LeaderId.voted_for` is a `pub` field of type `Option<NID>` on a
+  public type, its `Display` impl explicitly renders the `None` case, and the serde format
+  accepts `"voted_for": null` — so such values are publicly constructible and can arrive
+  from persisted state. `PartialOrd` panicking on representable values violates the
+  implicit no-panic expectation of comparison traits. `voted_for: None` is also the
+  natural representation of "no vote cast this term" in standard Raft. The crate itself
+  only constructs `Some(_)` internally, so this does not fire in the happy path — but any
+  user comparing a deserialized or hand-built `None` vote with an equal-term vote panics.
+- **Status:** pinned by `hegel_std_vote_partial_cmp_none_voted_for_panics` (fails
+  deterministically, every case hits the bug); sibling no-panic property excludes the
+  class with a cross-referencing comment. Not fixed, per instructions.
+
+### Observation (not asserted as a bug): duplicate ids overcount in `is_quorum`
+
+`BTreeSet::is_quorum`/`&[ID]::is_quorum` count each *occurrence* of a granted id
+(`count += 2` per iterator item), so passing a duplicated id (e.g. `[1, 1]` against config
+`{1, 2, 3}`) reports a quorum. All in-crate callers (`VecProgress`, `Membership`) pass
+unique ids, and the trait is `pub(crate)`, so this is out-of-domain today; the property
+tests therefore pass deduplicated granted sets. Worth a debug assertion or doc note
+upstream if the trait is ever made public.
+
+## Unsound properties abandoned
+
+- **Total order for `CommittedVote` with std leader ids** — `CommittedVote::cmp` unwraps
+  `partial_cmp`, which is `None` for equal-term committed votes with different
+  `voted_for`. That input is protocol-unreachable by design (a quorum can grant only one
+  leader per term), so a generator-level property asserting totality would be testing
+  outside the intended domain; skipped rather than filed as a bug.
+- **Validity of `next_coherent` output as a full `Membership`** — `next_coherent` alone
+  can produce voters without node entries (nodes are reconciled by `change()`), so
+  `ensure_valid()` was asserted only on `change()` results, and only config-level
+  properties on `next_coherent`.
+- No written property had to be weakened after a failure; the only failing test is the
+  real panic above.
+
+## Skill feedback
+
+- Smooth run: `cargo add --dev hegeltest -p openraft` on a nightly-2026-03-01 / edition
+  2024 workspace worked with no MSRV or naming friction; composites, `one_of!`,
+  `optional`, and drawing inside op loops all behaved as documented.
+- The "tests using fixed-seed RNGs are prime candidates" guidance paid off directly:
+  `vec_progress.rs` already had LCG-seeded model tests with a ready-made reference model,
+  and the hegel version was mostly a matter of routing the choices through `tc.draw` and
+  generating the quorum configurations too ("generate configurations, not just payloads").
+- The exhaustive-enumeration oracle for coherence (all 2^7 subsets as bitmasks) is a
+  pattern worth naming in the catalogue: for "for all quorums / for all subsets"
+  safety properties, a generated instance + exhaustive small-universe check is much
+  stronger than sampling both sides, and still fast (~16k bitmask intersections/case).
+- One repo-convention wrinkle: the target repo's CLAUDE.md mandates `make lint` (never
+  bare `cargo clippy`/`cargo fmt`), but that target builds unrelated OpenSSL-dependent
+  crates and fails in a hermetic environment; scoped `cargo clippy --no-deps -p openraft`
+  with the same `-D warnings` settings was the workable equivalent.
